{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779034356,"nonce":"K3Gzx3GAyj3IC8shTfGB5MjRWdw=","message":"### Chat sidebar scoping note: hide subagents until nested display exists\nIn the current unified chat sidebar, subagents are appearing as their own top-level project/group. That is misleading: subagents are part of the parent conversation/session structure and should eventually be folded under the parent that spawned them, with enough activity metadata to understand what they did.\n\nIssue 67a12d9 will hide subagent conversations from the top-level chat list for now. This is a UI containment choice, not a final data model decision. The durable implementation should identify parent/child session relationships at ingestion/runtime and expose a nested subagent view under the parent conversation, plus graph/live-agent affordances when those relationships are reliable.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}